------p2mBoundary7f3a9c2b
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="explanation"

The positive limit ensures f(H) / H^d is eventually positive, hence f(H) is positive for all sufficiently large H. The logarithm splits as log(f(H) / H^d) + d log(H); the first term has a finite limit and becomes negligible after division by H, while log(H) / H tends to zero.
------p2mBoundary7f3a9c2b
